<title>USA: Chile's ENAP buys Palanca, Oriente crudes for Sept.</title>
<headline>Chile's ENAP buys Palanca, Oriente crudes for Sept.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's state oil refiner Empresa Nacional del Petroleo (ENAP) bought Angolan Palanca and Ecuadoran Oriente crude cargoes in its latest purchase tender, trade sources said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The cargoes are scheduled to be delivered in the September 1-4 window.</p>
<p>A Swiss-based trading house sold 380,000 barrels of Oriente to ENAP at an undisclosed discount to West Texas Intermediate/Cushing, trade sources said.</p>
<p>A European company sold 950,000-960,000 barrels of Palanca to ENAP at a premium to Dated Brent.</p>
<p>The Chilean company purchased the same combination of crudes in its last tender for August delivery.</p>
<p>((--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
